diff --git a/packages/coding-agent/docs/acp.md b/packages/coding-agent/docs/acp.md
--- a/packages/coding-agent/docs/acp.md
+++ b/packages/coding-agent/docs/acp.md
@@ -28,3 +28,5 @@
 Client `mcpServers` entries connect over stdio or streamable HTTP. Their tools use the same exposure and `mcp__<server>__<tool>` namespace as local MCP servers. Local `mcp.json` entries and package registrations take precedence on name or namespace collisions. Client entries apply only to this session and are never saved to `mcp.json`. Connection failures produce warnings on stderr and do not stop session startup.
 
 ACP mode runs every tool with full permission. Tool calls are never sent to the client for approval. Connect only from clients and projects that you trust.
+
+`session/new` and `session/load` also publish `_meta.lody.modelCapabilities` version 1. Each authenticated model is keyed by its full `provider/model` ID and declares `effortValues` from the runtime's `getSupportedThinkingLevels` function. This lets clients show the selected model's own thinking levels before sending a prompt. `configOptions` still describe the current model; `session/set_config_option` returns its updated options after a model change. A model without reasoning declares `["off"]`, matching the native session control.
